    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_ed26d05841be0d2d176f542b97ebc19c9bc54c718a5062c41833b61f89808374",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Source fact: theta Mellin representation on the critical line becomes a real even integral. After x=e^{4u}, a frequency polynomial and constant obstruct a pure cosine transform. Theta reciprocity gives phi'(0)=-1/2, decay handles infinity, and two integrations by parts transfer the frequency factor into phi''-phi. Adding one-half e^u makes a theta-derived Phi even without changing Phi''-Phi. Interpretation: completion moves from frequency multiplication to kernel differentiation, and reciprocity supplies the needed boundary cancellation. Boundary: this constructs a transform but proves no sign changes; glyphs and scales are OCR-sensitive.",
