    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_874a26e0b669936b01c103fce4e00905d871a4aff93662c0b32892a58b55e577",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The lectures obtain the same zeta reflection through three distinct carriers: expanding the Hankel contour across the exponential kernel's imaginary pole lattice turns residues into zeta(1-s); Fourier-resolving the centered sawtooth summation error turns periodic cancellation into reciprocal modes and zeta(1-s); and Poisson summation turns Gaussian self-duality into theta reciprocity, whose split Mellin transform is explicitly symmetric in s and 1-s. Gamma and pi completion normalize these routes to the same functional equation without erasing their different convergence obligations.",
